{"title":"Career roadmap · Forensic Accounting Associate","role":"Forensic Accounting Associate","summary":"A Forensic Accounting Associate investigates financial records to identify fraud, financial irregularities, asset misappropriation, manipulation, disputes and other financial misconduct. A B.Com specialising in Forensic Accounting / Auditing is a strong direct foundation for this career.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1","Current degree":"B.Com (Bachelor of Commerce)","Course":"B.Com – Forensic Accounting / Auditing"},"about":[{"label":"Key combination","text":"Accounting + auditing + investigation + analytics + evidence"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Typical route"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Com Forensic Accounting/Auditing","Audit/Forensic Internship","Forensic Accounting Associate","Senior Associate","Manager","Senior Manager","Director / Partner"]}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career direction"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build accounting, audit, forensic investigation, Excel, SQL and data-analysis capabilities"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Become a specialist in fraud investigations, forensic audit, disputes, AML or financial crime"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Progress toward Forensic Manager, Investigation Manager, Risk/Financial Crime Manager or specialist roles"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Move into forensic leadership, expert advisory, partner/director roles, regulatory work or independent practice"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Accounting fundamentals"},{"text":"Financial accounting, business law"},{"text":"Complete accounting-cycle case"},{"text":"Accounting foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Auditing + E